        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can simplify the product of two square roots, such as <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}.]</span>\nFirst, we re-write the expression as a square:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2.]</span>\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 = 3.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We can simplify the product of two square roots, such as [MATH: \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}.]\nFirst, we re-write the expression as a square:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2.]\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 = 3.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can do something similar for a product of three cube roots, like <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}.]</span>\nFirst, we rewrite the expression as a cube:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3]</span>\nNow, recall that the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3 = 3.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We can do something similar for a product of three cube roots, like [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}.]\nFirst, we rewrite the expression as a cube:\n[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3]\nNow, recall that the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3 = 3.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nWe can simplify the product of two square roots, such as [MATH: \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}.]\nFirst, we re-write the expression as a square:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2.]\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 = 3.]\n\nContent:\nWe can do something similar for a product of three cube roots, like [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}.]\nFirst, we rewrite the expression as a cube:\n[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3]\nNow, recall that the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3 = 3.]"
