    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nWe can simplify the product of two square roots, such as [MATH: \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}.]\nFirst, we re-write the expression as a square:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2.]\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt{3}\\right)^2 = 3.]\n\nContent:\nWe can do something similar for a product of three cube roots, like [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}.]\nFirst, we rewrite the expression as a cube:\n[MATH: \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3}\\cdot \\sqrt[3]{3} = \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3]\nNow, recall that the cube and the cube root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt[3]{3}\\right)^3 = 3.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Simplifying Expressions Containing Square Root Surds\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: \\sqrt{5} \\cdot \\sqrt{5}].\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nFirst, we rewrite the expression as a square:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{5} \\cdot \\sqrt{5} = \\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^2]\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n[MATH: \\left(\\sqrt{5}\\right)^2 = 5.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: sqrt(6) \u22c5 sqrt(6).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 36]\nb. [MATH: 6]\nc. [MATH: sqrt(6)]\nd. [MATH: 12]\ne. [MATH: \u2212 36]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: sqrt(7) \u22c5 sqrt(7).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 7]\nb. [MATH: 2sqrt(7)]\nc. [MATH: 7]\nd. [MATH: sqrt(14)]\ne. [MATH: sqrt(7)]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Simplifying Expressions Containing Cube Root Surds\n\nExample Prompt:\nFind [MATH: \\sqrt[3]{12} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{12}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nGrouping up the square roots and the cube roots, we find\n[MATH: root(12, 3) \u22c5 sqrt(3) \u22c5 root(12, 3) \u22c5 sqrt(3) \u22c5 root(12, 3)|=; (root(12, 3) \u22c5 root(12, 3) \u22c5 root(12, 3))(sqrt(3) \u22c5 sqrt(3))|=; (root(12, 3))^{3}(sqrt(3))^{2}|=; 12 \u22c5 3|=; 36|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nFind the value of [MATH: root(\u2212 11, 3) \u22c5 root(\u2212 11, 3) \u22c5 root(\u2212 11, 3).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: \u2212 121]\nb. [MATH: 33]\nc. [MATH: 11]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 11]\ne. [MATH: 121]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nFind [MATH: root(\u2212 5, 3) \u22c5 sqrt(7) \u22c5 root(\u2212 5, 3) \u22c5 sqrt(7) \u22c5 root(\u2212 5, 3).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 35]\nb. [MATH: 49]\nc. [MATH: sqrt(25)]\nd. [MATH: \u2212 35]\ne. [MATH: 25]"
